  s grains have accumulated. Arm 3's figure is therefore a LOWER bound on the
  realistic cost; arm 4, at ten times the cadence, is the arm that actually
  resolves the trigger delta. Both are reported.
    NOTE - arm 5 bounds the SHARED COMPONENT'S PUBLIC CONTRACT, not Vorago's
  operating point: VoragoEngine runs one pre-render control step per 64-sample
  control chunk (vorago_engine.h:904-908), so it could issue at most one
  trigger per chunk even if the wiring were on - and it is not, OQ-1 is closed
  inert. Arm 5 issues 64 per chunk, the FR-019 cap, i.e. 48 000 birth attempts
  per second.
